window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Is joy something we seek, or something we make?</p> <p>In the eighth volume of the Xane series, author Mark White takes listeners on an emotional journey with Xane as she explores the concept of joy. Reflecting on her past experiences with fear, anger, sadness, shame, and contempt, Xane realizes she is ready to embrace joy. Guided by the Analyst, Xane learns that joy is not just about happiness but a deeper state of being—an open-hearted embrace of life and a sense of peace and connection.</p> <p>As Xane navigates her journey, she finds joy in her interactions with her bandmates—Leila, Ruby, Zoe, and Lena—and in the simple moments of life. The story delves into themes of vulnerability, connection, and self-acceptance, highlighting the importance of finding joy in the journey itself.</p> <p><i>Joy </i>is a powerful exploration of emotional intelligence, offering listeners a deeper understanding of joy and the complexities of human emotions. Join Xane as she discovers the beauty of living with an open heart and the joy that comes from being present in every moment.</p>"; 
